      statement: "dead-code-maybe --seeds all reports function-factory closures (e.g. register_analyzer.decorator, register_linker.decorator, register_def_use_extractor.decorator) and dict-config-style attributes (Cache.delete, TrackerSet.config, Store.config) as potentially dead. These are all dispatched through closure-factory or descriptor patterns the call-graph doesn't traverse"  # baa6
      root_cause: "Call-graph edge extraction doesn't model: (1) nested closures returned from factory functions and used as decorators, (2) descriptor protocol (property/staticmethod-like dispatch). Result: false-positive dead-code flags on the most-used dispatch primitives in the codebase. Compounds CCC dead-code FP issue with a specific structural cause"  # baa6
